  "conclusions": [
    "The accepted stored PMR Project bytes reach the known-project cache unchanged; the actual Media Tool chooser explicitly decodes them using CurrentMacMBCSEncodingToUTF16.",
    "The converter supplies selector 5 to EncodedToUTF16, which queries CFStringGetSystemEncoding and creates Unicode from the returned codec. No UTF-8-first trial or originating-code-page lookup occurs on this route.",
    "Projects_ListBox is concretely created as ATextListPane. Its actual UTF16 setter round-trips through current Mac legacy bytes, then stores UTF16 and reaches QString::fromUtf16 and QPainter::drawText.",
    "The bin Project column is distinct: FindProjectName resolves composition/source attributes, then uses the same current-Mac decoder before returning Unicode to Qt.",
    "Empty PMR Project may acquire current-project context; the chooser may also add the current project when absent.",
    "The separately run public CoreFoundation probe returned MacRoman and A7 -> U+00DF, agreeing with the user-confirmed Mac-created sharp-s project. This was not an in-process Media Composer observation.",
    "This establishes the native Mac decoder rule, not a universal source encoding for every historical PMR. Bella policy remains undecided; no production code changed."
  ],
